{
  "_comment": "pi: the folder `pi/agent` plays `~/.pi/agent`, so the only automatic root is pi/agent/sessions. Session A carries one measured response of every shape (durationMs, entry-timestamp fallback, error, aborted, a missing and a non-string stopReason, a zero-usage placeholder, a durationMs of 0), three side usages that count in totals only plus a tool result with usage, entries that never affect measurement, one entry without an id and two malformed lines. Session B is a clone: the copied entry older than the header minus 2 s is skipped by the copy cutoff, the copied entry inside that window is deduplicated by key, and only B's own response counts. Session C is an extension run sub-session; it attaches to A (`parentFile`) and counts as its own agent. `tailReads` start reading at byte `offset` (after two lines), so the header must still be read first. This file is separate from parser-expected.json because only the Windows tests read it until the macOS reader exists (METRICS 4.13).",
